@startuml
title UC 1.1: Create a New Job - Database Schema Design

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #ffe6cc
  BorderColor #d79b00
  BorderThickness 2
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #56517e
  BorderStyle dashed
  BackgroundColor transparent
}
skinparam ArrowColor #333333

rectangle "**Azure SQL Database 'job-details'**\n//Primary storage for Job Manager. Stores user-provided Job definitions//" as JM {

  class Job {
    + [PK] Id: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required)
    + UserId: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required)
    + Name: NVARCHAR(200) (required)
    + Description: NVARCHAR(1000) (optional)
    + Status: ENUM Active / Inactive / Deleted (required, soft delete)
    + ConcurrencyMode: ENUM Singleton / Concurrent (required)
    + Version: INT (required, starts at 1, +1 per edit)
    + CreatedAt: DATETIME2 (required, auto)
    + UpdatedAt: DATETIME2 (required, auto)
    --
    UQ (UserId, Name) WHERE Status <> Deleted
  }

  class JobSchedule {
    + [PK, FK] JobId: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required)
    + ScheduleType: ENUM OneTime / Recurring (required)
    + StartAt: DATETIME2 (required)
    + RepeatStepSize: INT (optional)
    + RepeatStepUnit: ENUM Minute / Hour / Day / Week / Month (optional)
  }

  class JobOutbox {
    + [PK] Id: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required)
    + [FK] JobId: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required)
    + EventType: ENUM JobCreated / JobUpdated / JobDeleted (required)
    + JobVersion: INT (required)
    + Payload: NVARCHAR(MAX) JSON (required, Job Snapshot)
    + CreatedAt: DATETIME2 (required, auto)
    + ProcessedAt: DATETIME2 (optional)
    + Attempts: INT (required, default 0)
    --
    IX (CreatedAt) WHERE ProcessedAt IS NULL
  }

  class JobLaunchDetails {
    + [PK, FK] JobId: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required)
    + Endpoint: NVARCHAR(2048) (required)
    + HttpMethod: ENUM GET / POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE (required)
    + Headers: NVARCHAR(MAX) JSON (optional)
    + Payload: NVARCHAR(MAX) JSON (optional)
  }

  Job "1" -- "1" JobSchedule : has
  Job "1" -- "1" JobLaunchDetails : has
  Job "1" -- "0..*" JobOutbox : emits
}

rectangle "**Azure SQL Hyperscale 'job-orchestrator'**\n//Primary storage for Job Orchestrator. Stores pre-calculated Job schedule snapshots//" as ORCH {

  class JobScheduleSnapshot #dae8fc {
    + [PK] JobId: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required, = Job.Id)
    + UserId: UNIQUEIDENTIFIER (required)
    + ConcurrencyMode: ENUM Singleton / Concurrent (required)
    + ScheduleType: ENUM OneTime / Recurring (required)
    + RepeatStepSize: INT (optional)
    + RepeatStepUnit: ENUM Minute / Hour / Day / Week / Month (optional)
    + NextRunAt: DATETIME2 (required)
    + LaunchDetails: NVARCHAR(MAX) JSON (required)
    + Status: ENUM Active / Inactive / Deleted (required)
    + Version: INT (required, = Job.Version)
    + CreatedAt: DATETIME2 (required)
    --
    IX (NextRunAt) WHERE Status = Active
  }
}

Job -[#6c8ebf,bold]right-> JobScheduleSnapshot : <b>is synchronized with</b>\n(via Outbox + idempotent REST)\n1 : 0..1, logical reference, no cross-DB FK

note as ISO
  <b>Isolation level: READ COMMITTED (RCSI)</b>
  <b>Job Manager:</b> one transaction inserts Job + JobSchedule +
  JobLaunchDetails + JobOutbox. It only inserts new rows and never reads
  then writes, so dirty, non-repeatable and phantom reads cannot affect it;
  Serializable / Snapshot would add locking cost with no benefit.
  UQ (UserId, Name) still takes key locks under RCSI -> 409 Conflict.
  <b>Job Orchestrator:</b> the snapshot upsert is applied only if
  incoming Version > stored Version, via INSERT + PK-violation fallback.
end note
JobLaunchDetails -[hidden]right- ISO
@enduml
